          "date": "2026-09-08 03:50:00.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-09-08 03:59:14.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-19605 lnet: push NI status change to peers",
        "message": "LU-19605 lnet: push NI status change to peers\n\nA node's per-NI status lives in its ping buffer, and ni_status points\ndirectly into that buffer. Peers only learn of a new status when we\npush to them, and lnet_peer_needs_push() only returns true when the\nping buffer sequence number has moved (or on a forced push). That\nsequence number is bumped only when the buffer is rebuilt, which is\nalso the only caller of lnet_push_update_to_peers() on a non-router.\n\nThe health-driven status transitions update *ni_status in place, so\nthe buffer contents change but its sequence number does not. Nothing\nqueues a push, and a peer keeps its stale cached lpni_ns_status until\nsome unrelated event rebuilds our ping buffer or the peer pings us\nagain. Routers are unaffected: lnet_check_routers() forces the push\nitself when lnet_update_ni_status_locked() reports a change.\n\nMark the ping buffer for update whenever lnet_ni_set_status() actually\nchanges the status, so that the monitor thread rebuilds it and pushes\nthe new state. lnet_mark_ping_buffer_for_update() only sets an atomic\nand signals the monitor thread, so it is safe to call from the health\npaths, which run under lnet_net_lock(). It is a no-op when routing is\nenabled, leaving the router path as it was.\n\nThis is what sanity-lnet test_236 checks, and why it fails with\n\"Expect peer NI state down\": the router never sees the local NI go\ndown after its health is set to 0.\n\nFixes: 3f423f8d4977 (\"LU-19476 lnet: Set local NI status based on health value\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nChange-Id: I82cd80e762709ed03038820f999d21eb02e7d9cd\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
